PASS A1b CONTROL: with five laws spread over 0-0.4 dex, 'some law fits MUSE-III's headline to 2 sigma' happens 42% of the time for a random datum (0.42): the match of D is what MUSE-III's number PICKS OUT, but finding SOME law that fits is unremarkable; the informative part is the flat/H(z) exclusion at 6-30 sigma, and MUSE-III is the record's non-diagnostic datum

